# THE OLD NAME, KEPT ALIVE AS A REDIRECT.
#
# liuxuesheng.io was the board's address for the whole of its first life, and
# that address is in places this repo cannot reach: invite links sent by
# WeChat, a message pasted into a group of two hundred agents, the last slide
# of a deck sent to Hong Kong, and the bio of an Instagram account. Turning it
# off would break every one of them silently — a tapped link that goes nowhere
# reads as the company being gone, not as the company having moved.
#
# So it answers forever and sends every path to the same path on the new name.
# `permanent` because it is: a 301 is cached by browsers and by WeChat, which
# is the point.
#
# ITS OWN FILE AND ITS OWN VARIABLE. Caddy substitutes one variable per
# address, and two site blocks sharing an address is a startup failure that
# takes down every other site on this box. TOMSCODING_BOARD_OLD_DOMAIN is set
# only while the old name still resolves; unset, this binds an internal
# .localhost that nothing points at and does nothing.
{$TOMSCODING_BOARD_OLD_DOMAIN:oldboard.localhost} {
	redir https://{$TOMSCODING_BOARD_DOMAIN}{uri} permanent
}

# AND ITS www, which had nowhere to go.
#
# The board's own www block moves to the new name with the board — that is what
# it is for — and the old www is then a hostname with a certificate, a DNS
# record and no site block anywhere on this box. Somebody who typed the name
# with a www in front of it, or a link written that way in a message two months
# ago, gets nothing.
#
# Same redirect, its own variable, for the same reason the block above has one:
# one variable per address, and a second block sharing an address is a startup
# failure that takes the box down.
{$TOMSCODING_BOARD_OLD_WWW:oldboardwww.localhost} {
	redir https://{$TOMSCODING_BOARD_DOMAIN}{uri} permanent
}
